        "completed_feedback_polynomial_identity_and_unique_algebraic_response"
      ],
      "scope_boundary": "Any bounded relative terminal response induced by two native pairing-preserving continuation arrows after m completed returns. Vanishing terminal freedom within this interface does not select the interface itself."
    },
    {
      "id": "R25.6",
      "title": "The event-horizon error is bounded without an external decay law",
